# Moxa ioLogik E1211.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | Moxa ioLogik E1211 Remote Ethernet I/O — 16-channel DO
# | 
# | Source: ioLogik E1200 Series User Manual V16.2, August 2025 (Appendix A)
# | Protocol: Modbus/TCP (port 502); Modbus/TCP ID default = 1
# | 
# | FC01 addr 0-15 (len 16): DO_status ch0-15 (0=OFF, 1=ON; R/W)
# | FC01 addr 16-31 (len 16): DO_pulseStatus ch0-15 (0=STOP, 1=START; R/W)
# | FC02 addr 4096-4111 (len 16): DO_p2pStatus ch0-15 (0=OFF, 1=ON; R)
# | FC02 addr 4112-4127 (len 16): DO_p2pSafeModeFlag ch0-15 (0=OFF, 1=ON; R)
# | FC01 addr 4128-4143 (len 16): DO_p2pSafeModeFlagClear (1=clear safe mode flag; R/W)
# | FC01 addr 4144 (len 1): watchdogAlarmFlag (1=clear watchdog alarm; R/W)
# | FC04 System: same as E1210 (modelName@5000, deviceUpTime@5020, lanMac@5024,
# | lanIp@5027, firmwareVersion@5029, firmwareBuildDate@5031, deviceName@5040)
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Moxa
@model=ioLogik E1211
@vendor_website=moxa.com
@description=16-DO remote Ethernet I/O, Modbus/TCP. FC01: DO_status ch0-15 (addr 0), DO_pulseStatus (addr 16). FC03: DO_all_statusFromDO-00 (addr 32), DO_pulseCount ch0-15 (addr 36-51), DO_pulseOnWidth ch0-15 unit 1ms (addr 52-67), DO_pulseOffWidth ch0-15 unit 1ms (addr 68-83). FC02: DO_p2pStatus (addr 4096), DO_p2pSafeModeFlag (addr 4112). FC01: DO_p2pSafeModeFlagClear (addr 4128), watchdogAlarmFlag (addr 4144).
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/moxa-iologik-e1211.toml; Source: ioLogik E1200 Series User Manual V16.2, August 2025 (Appendix A). Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
